WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.500
- Welcome everyone to another coffee break

00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:04.880
here on my channel Firm Learning,

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:07.150
Today we're a bit of an unusual location,

00:00:07.150 --> 00:00:09.520
here we are at the Eat and Style.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:11.040
We're invited by a friend of mine

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:13.730
who has a food startup
that we are going to visit,

00:00:13.730 --> 00:00:16.840
it's a food fair, so we
are very excited for that.

00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.710
But the topic of today

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:22.370
is going to be what is
called the Great Resignation,

00:00:22.370 --> 00:00:24.910
this trend of especially young people

00:00:24.910 --> 00:00:27.220
preferring now to work at home,

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:31.120
working very flexibly instead
of working in an office

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:33.720
needing to come into the
office on a regular basis.

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:36.600
I'm going to weigh into that,
give my opinion on that,

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.520
and especially I will talk about

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:40.570
whether I believe it is a good idea

00:00:40.570 --> 00:00:42.950
for people fresh out of university

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.150
in the first years of their career

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:48.210
to work in a job that is fully remote,

00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:50.740
to work somewhere where
they're not in direct contact

00:00:50.740 --> 00:00:53.380
with colleagues, but just
at home working from home,

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:55.670
whether this is a great idea or not.

00:00:55.670 --> 00:00:59.380
And as a small hint, I don't
think that it's a great idea.

00:00:59.380 --> 00:01:01.820
I know that this is a
little bit controversial,

00:01:01.820 --> 00:01:04.350
but we're going to dive
into this in a moment

00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:06.020
so stick in here with me.

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:08.260
I got the idea for this video this morning

00:01:08.260 --> 00:01:11.440
right in my LinkedIn feed
at this post from McKinsey

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:14.700
saying "Employees are
quitting in record numbers,

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:17.040
many without another role lined up.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.510
It's up to leaders to
respond to these trends

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:21.310
and re-engage the workforce

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:24.820
so organizations can
retain their best talent."

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:27.930
And this trend, this phenomena
that is described here

00:01:27.930 --> 00:01:30.770
is called the Great Resignation.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.170
It is widely described

00:01:32.170 --> 00:01:34.910
and apparently it's also backed up by data

00:01:34.910 --> 00:01:37.200
that since earlier this
year a lot of people

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.720
apparently much more than normal

00:01:38.720 --> 00:01:41.450
are resigning from their job,

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:44.130
and this is often linked
to the development

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:45.440
during the health situation

00:01:45.440 --> 00:01:47.920
that was going on since last year

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:51.290
and the thought process that
this triggered for many people.

00:01:51.290 --> 00:01:53.210
Apparently this is especially triggered

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:55.120
by millennials and Gen Z people

00:01:55.120 --> 00:01:58.250
that are not really satisfied
anymore with their job.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:01:59.910
And I couldn't confirm that, when talking

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.420
to people, friends, colleagues,

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:05.680
who tell me that they
don't wanna work anymore

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:07.910
in the same way that they used to work,

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:10.850
maybe before the situation since 2019.

00:02:10.850 --> 00:02:14.890
A big trend seems to be that
people do not want to work

00:02:14.890 --> 00:02:16.580
from an office anymore,

00:02:16.580 --> 00:02:20.130
that people want to work
remote, want to work from home

00:02:20.130 --> 00:02:21.750
and this full-time.

00:02:21.750 --> 00:02:24.850
And of course, I do see
many advantages to that.

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:27.370
Of course, especially
if you have a family,

00:02:27.370 --> 00:02:29.360
and another big plus that I see

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.490
is that often this gives you
a little bit more flexibility

00:02:32.490 --> 00:02:35.670
to on the side work on some
other project of yours,

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.680
some other passions that
you really want to follow.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:41.680
So for this let's hear it
from Johannes from SPICEWISE,

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:45.170
he's a Rocket Scientist
working a full-time job,

00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:47.550
and he started his passion project

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:49.850
during this time in the pandemic.

00:02:49.850 --> 00:02:52.070
So Johannes from SPICEWISE was kind enough

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:54.210
to invite us here today
to the Eat in Style,

00:02:54.210 --> 00:02:57.270
lots of amazing food, we
already also tried out yours,

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:58.750
pretty amazing stuff.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:00.710
So, the topic we already talked about it,

00:03:00.710 --> 00:03:02.630
the Great Resignation.

00:03:02.630 --> 00:03:04.060
That's pretty amazing because I think

00:03:04.060 --> 00:03:06.320
you did not resign from your full-time job

00:03:06.320 --> 00:03:07.670
with your project,

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:11.060
but it also had something to
do with the health situation,

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:12.070
is that correct?

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:16.120
- Yes, so thank you very much
for your time and visiting us

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:18.033
at our SPICEWISE booth.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:22.670
Yes, you're right, we
used the current situation

00:03:22.670 --> 00:03:25.000
together with my kindergarten friends

00:03:25.000 --> 00:03:27.670
to develop a natural supplement,

00:03:27.670 --> 00:03:30.350
and we did it, yeah part time.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:34.880
So, we all three, we stayed
in our full-time jobs,

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:38.250
yeah, tried to perform very good,

00:03:38.250 --> 00:03:41.970
but also used for example the
extra time during lockdown

00:03:41.970 --> 00:03:44.860
where you cannot go out to
the cinema or whatsoever

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.130
to develop a product or in this case,

00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:51.763
particular case three products.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:56.600
Yeah, and fulfill our childhood dream

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:01.600
to, yeah, develop and found the company,

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:05.130
and yeah, today you are here
at our booth of SPICEWISE

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:07.110
and this is the result.

00:04:07.110 --> 00:04:08.070
- That's pretty amazing,

00:04:08.070 --> 00:04:09.680
and this, what I
understand this whole move

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.680
we know of the Great
Resignation what it's all about,

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:14.740
people in a full-time job asking
themselves, what can we do?

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:16.300
What is really our passion?

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.370
What are some projects we want to pursue?

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:20.570
And is it correct that
you did this fully remote?

00:04:20.570 --> 00:04:21.930
So really also an example of working

00:04:21.930 --> 00:04:23.480
completely from home?
- Yes.

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:25.630
- How did this team of
yours work together?

00:04:26.652 --> 00:04:29.490
- So the team is spread through Germany,

00:04:29.490 --> 00:04:31.780
so we have someone Wurzburg,
someone in Stuttgart,

00:04:31.780 --> 00:04:33.870
and me in Munich.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.640
And during the lockdown we
was not able to come together

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:39.410
to work in a kind of a
workshop or whatsoever.

00:04:39.410 --> 00:04:43.300
Also our suppliers needed
to work fully remote.

00:04:43.300 --> 00:04:47.350
So, actually it was a very great workflow

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:51.500
because we start I think
to invest more time

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.010
in during August/September 2020.

00:04:54.010 --> 00:04:55.690
From my point of view,

00:04:55.690 --> 00:04:58.763
it was very, very good
and a great flow, yeah.

00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:00.510
- Thanks, that awesome.

00:05:00.510 --> 00:05:03.210
If you are also interested
in this SPICEWISE products

00:05:03.210 --> 00:05:05.810
I will link a link in
the video description

00:05:05.810 --> 00:05:07.090
to their products, so check it out,

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:08.590
trust it is really amazing.

00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.120
Thank you Johannes, much appreciated.

00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:11.483
- Thank you very much, good bye.

00:05:11.483 --> 00:05:14.230
- This for sure is quite
an inspirational story,

00:05:14.230 --> 00:05:16.420
and of course this begs the question,

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:18.000
that if you are young professional,

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.230
someone fresh out of university,

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:22.510
should you choose your first job

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.970
to be a job that is fully remote,

00:05:24.970 --> 00:05:27.150
that gives you all this flexibility?

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:28.920
And apparently this is something

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.840
that many young graduates
currently are contemplating a lot,

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.430
and that also led to
this Great Resignation,

00:05:34.430 --> 00:05:37.050
this trend that we talked
about in the beginning.

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:39.890
And frankly while I understand
that it's already popular

00:05:39.890 --> 00:05:42.030
and while I do see the advantages,

00:05:42.030 --> 00:05:44.330
I think it is not a good idea.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:47.830
This is my humble
opinion on this question.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:50.010
And let me share three reasons with you

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:52.900
why I believe that
especially as a new joiner,

00:05:52.900 --> 00:05:54.200
as a young professional,

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:56.270
you should rather look for a job

00:05:56.270 --> 00:05:58.380
that is a bit more in this way,

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.470
that allows you to work from the office

00:06:00.470 --> 00:06:02.010
and get this experience this way.

00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:03.870
The first point is that I hold

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:06.380
that a significant part of the learnings

00:06:06.380 --> 00:06:07.990
that you get from a job

00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:11.970
in the first years of your
career is by observation,

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:15.100
by sitting in the office and
maybe over hearing a phone call

00:06:15.100 --> 00:06:17.880
that maybe a colleague has,
who's sitting next to you,

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:20.387
and this colleague maybe
just has a client call,

00:06:20.387 --> 00:06:24.020
a call with the client and
whole call is a bit difficult,

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:26.090
doesn't go the way the person planned,

00:06:26.090 --> 00:06:29.210
and you're just observing
what this person is doing

00:06:29.210 --> 00:06:31.850
in order to handle the
situation in the right way.

00:06:31.850 --> 00:06:35.200
On the same way observing how
some of the senior leaders

00:06:35.200 --> 00:06:38.460
who you just meet in the office,
handle certain situations,

00:06:38.460 --> 00:06:41.020
interact and engage with
the other colleagues,

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:43.440
with clients, with suppliers.

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.090
Observations that are not crucial,

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:49.410
that are not directly linked
to your day-to-day activities

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:52.250
are an extremely rich source of learning

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.570
that you will just really
not be able to tap into

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:57.370
by just sitting in front
of your desk at home,

00:06:57.370 --> 00:06:59.670
joining some occasional video conferences,

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:01.300
you will miss this for sure.

00:07:01.300 --> 00:07:03.090
The second point is on visibility.

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:05.410
Your visibility will for sure suffer

00:07:05.410 --> 00:07:07.430
if the only way other colleagues see you

00:07:07.430 --> 00:07:09.130
is if they join a video conference

00:07:09.130 --> 00:07:10.620
where you are part of as well.

00:07:10.620 --> 00:07:11.730
And if you're not really familiar

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:13.600
with this concept of visibility,

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:16.540
I do hope that it is one of
the most important concepts

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:18.920
to understand especially in
the first years of your career

00:07:18.920 --> 00:07:21.410
to succeed, I will link
another video above here

00:07:21.410 --> 00:07:24.040
where I talked about this
in details, so check it out.

00:07:24.040 --> 00:07:25.880
But for sure if you're sitting at home,

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.460
you're missing the opportunity
of meeting other people

00:07:28.460 --> 00:07:31.740
in the office, having an
informal coffee with them,

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:33.530
picking up things that are going on

00:07:33.530 --> 00:07:35.000
where you can be a part of,

00:07:35.000 --> 00:07:37.340
where you can increase your visibility,

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:40.930
this will not benefit your
long-term career progression

00:07:40.930 --> 00:07:42.140
in an organization.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:44.220
The third point is about opportunity.

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:47.220
I know many companies are in
a bit of a weird situation

00:07:47.220 --> 00:07:48.670
where part of the workforce

00:07:48.670 --> 00:07:50.780
is in the office on a regular basis,

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:52.320
while the other part of the workforce

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.190
is mainly working from home.

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:57.140
Also because in many
organizations, to some extent

00:07:57.140 --> 00:08:00.110
is up to the discretion of
the individual employees

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:02.550
whether they wanna come
to the office or not.

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.890
And I would argue that
in these organizations,

00:08:04.890 --> 00:08:07.340
the people who are not
regularly in the office

00:08:07.340 --> 00:08:09.630
have some significant disadvantages.

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:11.630
Now try to put yourself into the shoes

00:08:11.630 --> 00:08:14.280
of a team leader or the
leader in this organization,

00:08:14.280 --> 00:08:16.070
the person sitting in the office

00:08:16.070 --> 00:08:18.450
and has now a couple of things
to discuss with other people

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.360
or an idea the person now wants

00:08:20.360 --> 00:08:21.910
to work with with another person.

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:23.500
What is the person that this leader

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:25.420
will be most likely to reach out to?

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:28.313
And I would argue that
most likely this person

00:08:28.313 --> 00:08:31.570
will reach out to a colleague
who is sitting in the office,

00:08:31.570 --> 00:08:32.980
next to him or her,

00:08:32.980 --> 00:08:35.050
to whom this colleague
can directly reach out

00:08:35.050 --> 00:08:37.700
to discuss a certain
thing with that person,

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:40.210
and then often this leads to
some follow-up activities,

00:08:40.210 --> 00:08:43.333
maybe a whole new project
that this person can now lead

00:08:43.333 --> 00:08:47.280
because he was present, he
was there, he was available

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:50.360
to discuss these things with this leader.

00:08:50.360 --> 00:08:52.510
So while I fully acknowledge
that working from home,

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.940
working in a remote position

00:08:53.940 --> 00:08:55.930
has some significant advantages,

00:08:55.930 --> 00:08:58.440
I don't think it's the
best move you can do

00:08:58.440 --> 00:09:00.380
if you really want to grow as a person

00:09:00.380 --> 00:09:01.730
and as a professional.

00:09:01.730 --> 00:09:04.340
I trust that not everyone
will have my opinion on this

00:09:04.340 --> 00:09:06.410
and this is of course completely okay.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:08.230
So let me know, what is your opinion?

